WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.100
While the Galactic Empire expanded its power

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.730
and began absorbing neighboring star systems,

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:12.320
some of the outer frontier planets
maintained independent governments.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.870
The third planet in Tau Ceti system,
Sea of the Morningstar,

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.490
was a newly settled frontier planet.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.870
As with most newly settled planets,

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.410
once generations passed and its population increased,

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.460
relations with its overseer, the Stellar Alliance, worsened.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.590
And a war of independence began.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.800
To complement their meager fleet,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.090
the government of Sea of the Morningstar

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.930
issued a new type of edict,

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.430
the Letter of Marque.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:39.760
Letter of Marque

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.350
Papers in hand, space pirates attacked Stellar Alliance vessels,

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:47.810
greatly contributing to the revolution's success.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:52.030
This story begins more than one hundred years later.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.030
Time for some piracy!

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.870
Jamming remains strong.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.960
All radar systems still off-line.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.710
Very well done...

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:46.220
I'm told that these pirates have
a new captain, a young girl.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.830
There hasn't been a female
pirate since Blaster Ririka.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.230
I'd love to see her.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.690
And there we go.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.400
Video footage from the enemy ship!

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.990
Top-rate service.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.240
Nice work.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.420
I'm the captain of the space pirate ship Bentenmaru,

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.050
Captain Marika.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.300
Silence!

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.050
Or do you want to be torn apart
by Captain Marika's big guns?

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:29.680
Now, hand over your gold,

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.440
money, and other valuables...

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.330
I wonder how things are going for Chiaki...

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:57.170
Worry about your own ship, not hers.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.460
Right.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.630
What's our situation?

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.300
Same as ever!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.010
Thick dust, rough gravity waves...

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.300
And this is all we get, even with radar at max power?!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.310
Flying a spaceship here is absolutely insane!

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.930
I'm sorry.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.310
It's the perfect place for a ghost ship to appear.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.180
There's a break in the storm -3 minutes, 2 seconds off the bow.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.690
Elevation, +1 degree and 2 minutes.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.230
Get us there!

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.480
Output's stable...

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.200
All ready!

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.990
Roger!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.710
This is a break?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.210
It's not a stable space at all.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:48.100
You'd have to be a miner of rare ores or
an explorer to venture into these seas.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.260
Firing recon probes.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.640
The wind's going to get stronger.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.350
Keep us on course!

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.470
Gotcha!

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.810
Output rising!

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.030
We won't be retrieving those,

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.360
I'm sorry to say.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.290
We can't worry about our probes right now.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.330
Just gather as much data as you can.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.410
Um...

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:24.960
The Serenity Royal Family will
compensate you for your expenses...

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.880
Sure, that's great for later.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:31.890
But the problem is that our search
becomes much less efficient without any.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.180
I hope we can find it before then...

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.020
It's all right.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.980
If it's needed, the ghost ship will come to me.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.990
If it's needed, huh?

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.940
It's almost time.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.490
Right.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.540
Okay, thanks, you two.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.490
W-What?

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.540
That completes the hours that
minors are allowed to work.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.000
Both of you, grab some food and get to bed.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.010
Me too?

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.090
It's included in the Hakuoh Academy rules.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:12.300
Students are limited to an eight-hour work day.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.470
So...

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.310
Let's eat!

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.310
Sorry...

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:26.730
We don't have a personal chef to cook.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:28.020
But it's pretty good.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.110
I'm not concerned about the food.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:37.410
Everyone's searching for the ghost ship,
while I'm just sitting here, relaxing.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.290
That's...

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.250
Is it bothering you?

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.290
Yeah.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:47.300
I'm supposed to be the captain,
but the adults are still protecting me.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.880
So it's the same for you, Princess?

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:53.590
Oh, I'm sorry I compared myself to you!

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.520
No, I'm happy.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.980
For someone to say they're like me.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.440
That makes me very happy.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:08.440
I wonder what Chiaki is doing now...

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.280
No way... I'm not enjoying this!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.040
Maybe I'll adjust this part a little bit.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.420
We go from here to here, and then set a course...

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.350
So the captain's battle is tomorrow, huh?

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.020
Okay.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.110
One more time then.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.010
Morning!

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.590
Huh?

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.260
A bakery?

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.640
Sorry...

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.810
I've gotten accustomed to eating here.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.980
I've been staying up all night.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.060
All night?

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.310
You haven't experienced this before, have you?

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:35.870
When things get really busy,
we stay on the bridge all night.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.870
Then shouldn't I have stayed here too?

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:44.370
The Bentenmaru isn't in such bad shape
that it requires its underage captain here overnight.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.500
You just make the decisions when you need to!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.250
Relaxing is part of your job.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.500
Right...

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.340
So, what's the situation?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.260
I'll give you the abridged version.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:03.050
There are numerous observation buoy arrays,
set here by the Serenity search teams,

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:05.010
which are still active.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:10.900
Between the seventeen search teams they created
a fairly wide observation network over the years,

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:14.320
which continues to compile detailed data.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.900
Isn't that awfully lucky?

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.320
And the authorization code?

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:21.570
You should need a royal authorization code to access them.

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:23.330
Why didn't you wake me?

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:25.710
Well...

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.500
We cracked it.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.620
Easy as pie.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:30.590
What?!

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:36.210
Of course, it took a lot of prep work.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.590
Especially in the middle of this storm.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:42.390
It kept Schnitzer and Hyakume up all night.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.640
They finally went to sleep a little while ago.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.190
So that's where they are.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.440
But it's strange...

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:53.230
Search team 17 occurred fifteen years ago.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.820
And the princess is...

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.650
Thirteen.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:58.610
Yup.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.110
Using your authorization code

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.820
on a network that dates from
before your birth is pointless.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.990
But I entered it anyway, just in case.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:07.330
Your full name and biometrics.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.660
And it worked.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.120
Yep. Just like that.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.080
A name and genetic pattern that works,

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.290
regardless of when it's used.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.090
I guess the royal family may really be special.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:22.050
Are you born that way?

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.930
I believe so.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:30.900
That is why the royal family was able
to maintain Serenity's independence.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.690
Well, um, how's the network doing?

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:37.980
Find any data on the ghost ship?

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:40.360
The difference is like night and day.

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:43.370
See how clear it is?

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.330
Huh?

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.080
What's this?

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.330
Not sure, but they're probably multiple spaceships.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.330
Battleship-class.

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.670
They want the same thing we do.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.500
I was going to trade places
with Chiaki and slip away...

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.340
But apparently, it won't work.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.420
What should we do?

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:02.340
Pursue them?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.220
Not now.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.930
They're not close enough to worry about.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.970
If we want the same thing,
we'd just end up fighting.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:09.970
Roger.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:13.600
Okay, then I'll keep analyzing the data.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.900
Thanks.

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:22.900
What's up?

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:23.900
What's going on?

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:25.120
I'm checking right now.

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:31.250
Observation buoys 15 to 78 have
detected a major spatial irregularity.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.000
It's huge.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.380
Six light years away?

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.000
Let's go.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.040
Fast decisions.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.220
That's how a captain should act.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.470
Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.220
Is an accurate jump even possible in this weather?

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.430
We'll be slightly off our course.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:50.140
Fine by me.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:53.900
I'm sure you've realized this,
but that other fleet might have seen us.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.600
Then ready us for battle too.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:57.400
Roger.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.360
Prepare for hyperspace jump.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.990
Ghost ship, here we come!

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:47.360
Given the rough weather,
I'm amazed we made it out safely.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.280
We aren't safe!

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.000
The alarms are blaring because we aren't safe!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.700
I'm seeing fusion blasts,
small ones, on the ship's hull.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.750
If one of those got inside the ship, we'd be done for!

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:03.630
The missiles I launched ahead have
become misaligned with the Bentenmaru.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.800
It'll work next time.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.760
I have the data for corrections.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.300
Next time, we'll be somewhere else!

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:13.100
We are not in such danger that you need to panic.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.440
Stop whining.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:25.610
What's going on?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:30.530
We fired some anti-matter missiles
to clear out the stardust,

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:31.820
but they were slightly out of alignment.

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:33.370
I see...

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.000
So where's our treasure?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.370
The explosions still haven't died down.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.460
Wait a second.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.000
This is a mess.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.460
Stormy space, huh?

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.670
Hang on...

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:51.680
This spatial irregularity doesn't originate here.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.720
It's interference from some other space region.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.100
Another space region?

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.350
Should we go there?

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:00.230
The source is in motion.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:04.610
As it moves, the spatial irregularity is fading.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:05.560
Can we follow it?

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:08.990
Nope. We can't catch it from normal space.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.030
No good, huh?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.450
Not a total loss.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:17.370
If I align the data we just received with
what we got from the observation buoys,

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.880
I should be able to predict the next irregularity.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:23.460
We can't get ahead of it,
but we'll be able to follow faster.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:26.630
Now what?

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:27.930
I figured they'd show up.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:30.090
It's a different energy signal this time.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.800
Radar signals detected.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.930
All crew to battle stations!

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.140
Did they see us?

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:50.660
We're pretty far. Probably not.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.650
I think there are two energy signatures there.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:57.620
Our sensors are at maximum sensitivity,
so we were able to spot them.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.370
But the Bentenmaru is in passive scanning mode,

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:03.620
so its energy radiation is reduced,
and they shouldn't have seen us yet.

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:04.500
But...

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.710
Once they begin active scanning, they'll find us.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:08.670
Can we slip past?

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.890
There's another radar signal.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.120
Sorry, we can't escape.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.140
I'm reading a cross field.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:17.050
A cross field?

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:20.390
Radar scanning over the same space
from two different directions.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.900
Basically, using radar from two sides.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.060
Launching decoys.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:25.650
Go!

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:33.780
I plotted a random course to confuse them.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.240
But if they're careful enough to use a cross field,

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.410
I don't know whether a decoy will be effective.

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:42.750
There's a third signal.

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:49.130
They probably split their fleet in advance,
prior to returning to normal space.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:52.590
They know how to use numbers to their
advantage, so they're going to be tough.

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.670
Heavy storms...

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.600
A fleet split into multiple groups.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.350
The closest one is...

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.180
It's signal 2!

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:02.350
An escort-class.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.430
Probably two of them.

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:05.140
Our relative speed is negative.

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.070
They're accelerating, on an approach course.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.400
Understood.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:12.320
No more running.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.280
Reverse course.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.740
Roger that!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:22.620
Before we go, let's greet the two nearest ships.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:25.630
All crew, prepare for anti-ship warfare.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.460
What are your orders?

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.590
Shall we launch the first shot?

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.880
Or wait for them to fire?

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.340
It doesn't matter whether they plan to fire or not.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.390
Get as close as possible,

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:42.010
then fire a fully charged dispersal shot.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:46.680
She's going to damage their sensors and armor
to prevent them from following us.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.520
Smart.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.150
The blood of Captain Kato flows through her.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.040
The blood of the captain...

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:02.040
Okay, ready anytime you are!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.540
Bentenmaru, let's go!

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:13.300
To approach this close in anti-ship combat is unheard of.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.340
Jamming initiated!

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:16.630
Don't mess this up.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:17.550
Leave it to me.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.630
Engines to full!

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:21.140
We'll head straight through them!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:26.310
We don't have to jump directly into
<i>both</i> of their firing ranges...

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.810
We'll win because we're doing it.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:32.550
Turret 1, target alpha on starboard.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.530
Turret 2, target bravo on portside.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.030
The attack will proceed as planned.

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:39.700
A full blast at our closest point.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:43.290
Ready targeting in advance.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.700
Enemy ships identified.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:48.420
They're Corback-class escorts. Serenity ships.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.460
No way!

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:51.670
No change to our plan.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.460
We fire regardless of whether they do too.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:55.880
Roger.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:05.680
Energy readings rising!

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:06.640
Here it comes!

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.280
Quickly withdraw!

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:35.460
Are they following?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:36.710
Nope.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.920
They didn't expect us to fire once and withdraw.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:43.220
If we'd been serious about fighting,
we'd have done something smarter.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.840
Roger.

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:46.890
Did our beams hit them?

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.640
They did.

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.430
Even if we didn't penetrate their armor,

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:54.440
we've badly damaged their sensor arrays
and surveillance equipment.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.230
Okay.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:59.860
Next time, they'll come after us for real...

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:01.620
Um...

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:06.620
Is it too late to contact those Corbacks?

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:08.990
Why?

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:11.630
If I tell them I'm on board...

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.880
If they're Serenity ships,

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.130
they shouldn't be targeting us.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:19.760
Please let me contact them.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.050
Not now.

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:25.760
This is a misunderstanding!

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:29.980
Otherwise, a Serenity ship would never fire on me!

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:33.180
We must correct the confusion as soon as we can!

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:37.230
Coorie, has anyone tried to contact the Bentenmaru?

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:41.110
No hails, no FTL comms.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:46.530
After that last skirmish, they know who we are.

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:49.240
But they haven't attempted contact.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.950
You know what that means, right, Gruier?

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.740
It's all a misunderstanding!

00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:55.340
If they knew I'm on board...

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:00.380
If it's a misunderstanding,

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.340
things should go better next time we run into them.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.760
But I'm sorry...

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.970
The Bentenmaru is a pirate ship.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:10.850
We have to consider the enemy's logic.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.430
But...

00:20:12.430 --> 00:20:14.600
Right now, you're supposed to be aboard

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:18.650
a Hakuoh Academy practice cruise.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.700
And the Bentenmaru should be engaged in its usual piracy.

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:29.910
The fact that you're on this ship
is a powerful card in any negotiation.

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.460
So please keep it in reserve.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:38.460
You are Princess Gruier Serenity, right?

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:44.720
Very well.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.720
Thank you, Captain.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:50.810
I...

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.230
I'm glad I came to this ship.

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:00.730
I can see it.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.870
Captain, tell us our course please!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:17.700
Now that we know the Serenity Fleet
is searching for the ghost ship in force,

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:19.170
we won't waste any more time.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.920
So what do we do?

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:23.250
What else?

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.180
We act like pirates.

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:27.720
We pursue the Serenity Fleet,

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.010
beat them to it,

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:31.260
and take a piece of the action!

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.010
So cool...

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:35.020
I'm shivering.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.910
Is that acceptable, Gruier?

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:39.770
It's cowardly.

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:46.020
But I believe we shall be able to justify ourselves later.

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:47.030
Make it so.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.030
Leave it to me!

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:52.160
Let's go, everyone!

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.540
Roger!

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.300
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:11.640
Battle in the Storm

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:12.510
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:18.020
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:21.020
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:24.400
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.490
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:30.530
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:39.460
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:44.340
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:48.170
How far?

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.840
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:54.470
Until the end.

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:55.810
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:59.140
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:07.990
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:11.740
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.160
What should we do?

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:16.330
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:20.620
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:26.670
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.930
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:39.050 --> 00:23:40.640
A quake occurs in space-time,

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:44.150
and impossible amounts of light
and shockwaves rock the ship.

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:48.360
A pirate's weapons are their own skills
and their captain's decisions.

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:53.820
As the ghost ship appears, two princesses face off.

00:23:54.650 --> 00:23:56.120
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:58.010
Wanderer of light.

00:23:58.010 --> 00:23:59.000
Look forward to it.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.000
Wanderer of Light

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.510
Pursue, beat them to it,
and take a piece of the action!
